<title>BELGIUM: RESEARCH ALERT - Befimmo a 'buy'.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Befimmo a 'buy'.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of research report -</p>
<p>Co name-----------Sector------Price------Broker-------------</p>
<p>    Befimmo	     Real estate 2,240  *   Vermeulen Raemdonck</p>
<p>COMMENT: Sicafi Befimmo provides better liquidity than alternative real estate investments (direct, certificates). This vehicle is particularly attractive for individuals as dividends are subject to the reduced 15 percent withholding tax in full discharge of personal income tax. Befimmo assets are of the highest quality: most buildings are virtually new and located in first choice sites.</p>
<p>Prospects are rather flat, no rent growth expected in the short run, save inflation. On the other hand, the real estate market has been stagnating at the bottom for some time now and it seems it can only pick up. The only question is when. We suggest a 'buy' rating for the attractive yield and the quality of the underlying assets.</p>
<p>Analyst: Jean-Marc Temple, telephone: 32 2 547 70 95</p>
<p>(*) Date of research report: June 18</p>
<p> Estimates:   EPS	  pvs est   P/E     Dividend</p>
<p> 1997	   154 BFR    (n/a)     14.5    5.6 pct yld</p>
<p> 1998	   166 BFR</p>
